Z||000000||hugh||10-27-2001||05:02 PM||||Here's the story:<BR>  Tomcat is getting an 88 GT,he plans on racing it and may need some help in the form of advice,encouragement,Ideas.He is from Connecticut,if there are any members from his area,maybe even some manual help.He did some racing 30 years ago,but has been in a wheelchair for the past 30 years.He plans on using hand controls,and I'm sure if there is any way someone on this forum can help him get some kind of power steering it will make a big difference.His son is going to be setting the car up and might be able to use some of our help.I can't think of anything better than having a car driven by Tom pulling into the winners spot with our logo on it.I posted this without anything more than Tom's permission to let you know he is in a wheelchair.All the rest is my idea,and I hope he doesn't mind that I've taken upon myself to ask you to give him any help you can. ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Nashco||10-27-2001||05:19 PM||||Hmm....who wants to put some thought into a paddle shifter design?  Sounds like fun to me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It'd also take some force feedback braking and throttle controls, which are easy enough.  Maybe we could turn to Lawrence of <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebElectric Magazine</A> for some help.  Sounds like some fun electronics and maybe we could figure out the paddle shifter.  What do you guys think?  I'm a Mechanical Engineering student, and this sounds like something I would definitely help with.  I'd love a paddle shifter for my car!  It'd take some good adaptation skills to make it work for a non-sequential gearbox, unless we used an automatic with a hard-shifting valve body.<P>What kind of racing are we talking?  SCCA, oval track, or what?  I'm assuming scca or the equivalent.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
