Z||000003||tomcat06085||10-27-2001||05:39 PM||||hey Hugh...i borrowed a picture for my signature, think its FieroKyle's, hope he doesn't mind...my son has me exercising and getting in shape for the springtime. He's a big Pontiac fan and must have four or five GTO's and LeMans vintage 1970-71. Anyway, my goals are set and we're hoping to have me and the car ready for next season of local autocross and some LimeRock. He's finishing up a 40 ft by 80 ft building in Winsted, CT and after he's settled in, he'll start working on the handcontrol layout and power steering. He said digital servo units for brake and gas would be much more dependable and easier to use than the mechanical unit that bolts to the steering column. I've been driving all sorts of stuff with handcontrols for thirty years....'74 Buick, '70 Cougar XR7 351 HP, '73 Plymouth Satalite/Sebring, '85 Dodge Van B250, '98Dodge Grand Caravan by EnterVan ( a Chrysler/Braun Enterprise )..loved them all.<P>I'm planning on racing in the stock street class with the minor mods that club racing allows...if I can be competitive, we'll do some lowering and stiffening, better springs, shocks, sway bars, maybe some engine work, racing rubber. My cousin Bob said he could get the car up here in the next week or so. I'm really looking forward to it...should be challenging and fun. We're gonna trailer it, sowe'll be looking for an 18 or 20 foot trailer with electric brakes. <P>Thanks for plug...I'll need all the help I can get. Also, thanks for the great deal on the 88 GT.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://jrreeves.com/images/blckfire.jpg"> <BR>tomcat...Thanks for the help!||||reg||7
